 "diagnosis": "The invariant 'sum >= 0' is too weak. After the loop, Dafny knows sum >= 0 and i > a || i > b, but cannot easily derive sum >= 1 (needed for sum != 0). The key insight is that since a > 0 and b > 0, the loop body always executes at least once with i=1, and since 1 divides everything, sum gets incremented by at least 1. We need a stronger invariant like 'i == 1 || sum >= 1' that captures this: at entry i==1 so it holds vacuously; after the i=1 iteration sum >= 1 and i=2; and sum only grows from there."}

